  "title": "What If You Opened All 85 Billion Pokémon Cards?",
  "description": "Pokémon has made over 85 billion cards.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Pok%C3%A9mon Trading Card Game: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Trading_Card_Game\n\nFrom Wikipedia (Pokémon Trading Card Game): as of March 2026 the game has produced over 85 billion cards worldwide; the PSA 10 Pikachu Illustrator, the most expensive Pokémon card ever sold, was bought for $5,275,000 in July 2021 and sold for $16.5 million in February 2026. Our math: 85 billion seconds is about 2,693 years (365.25-day years), a day has 86,400 seconds; $16.5M / $5.275M is about 3.1. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #pokemon #pokemoncards #whatif #howtheymakemoney",
